# Changelog

The main changes to Ethereum Dashboard since the revamp started, newest first. Each entry is one phase,
dated by its merge into main. Full details, checklists and the reasons behind each change are in PHASEPLAN.md.

## Phase 6: Polish & Growth (2026-10-08)

### Added
- End-to-end tests (Playwright) for lookup, connect, revoke, swap, send, wrap, contract calls, alerts and the
  installable app, on desktop and phone sizes, against local Anvil chains running the real Uniswap v3 contracts.
  Runs in CI.
- Installable app (PWA): manifest, icons, service worker and an offline page.
- Browser notifications as a fourth alert channel (Web Push, free VAPID keys), and a notification when a
  transaction confirms in a background tab.
- REST API (`POST /api/v1/tools/{name}`) using the MCP server's API keys and daily quota; `/docs` and an
  OpenAPI 3.1 spec (`/api/openapi.json`) generated from the Zod schemas.
- `sitemap.xml`, `robots.txt` and share images with live data for transaction, address and token pages.
- Privacy-safe product analytics: named events to Umami and, optionally, PostHog (no addresses, hashes or amounts).

### Changed
- Read-only pages (governance, L2s, DeFi, ETH supply, staking, blobs, MEV, derivatives, homepage cards) render on
  the server and stream in, instead of loading in the browser.
- `API_RATE_LIMIT` sets the per-IP rate limit (default 120 requests a minute).

## Phase 5: On-Chain Actions (2026-10-07)

### Added
- One transaction flow for every action: build, simulate (`eth_simulateV1`), plain-English preview with balance
  changes, fee and GoPlus warnings, sign in the user's own wallet, track until confirmed. The app never holds keys.
- Swaps (`/swap`) through Uniswap v3, quoted on-chain with no API key.
- Send (`/send`), staking with Lido and Rocket Pool and wrap/unwrap (`/stake`).
- Approvals manager (`/approvals`): revoke one or up to 8 approvals at once.
- Contract explorer (`/contract`): read and write any verified contract (Etherscan or Sourcify ABIs, proxies followed).
- ENS manager (`/ens-manager`): register, renew, set primary name and edit records.

### Not included
- Bridges (optional): left out because the bridge API couldn't be tested safely.

## Phase 4: AI Layer (2026-10-07)

### Added
- MCP server (`/api/mcp`) with 20 read-only tools for Claude, Cursor and other MCP clients; personal API keys
  (stored hashed) with 200 calls a day each; `/mcp` setup page.
- "Ask ETH Dashboard" assistant on every page (Groq free tier) that knows the connected wallet, plus Explain
  buttons on transaction, contract and token pages.
- Guardrails: tools are read-only, on-chain text is treated as data, never asks for keys or seed phrases.

### Changed
- Market Insights no longer scrapes with Firecrawl; it uses CoinGecko, DefiLlama, derivatives and staking data directly.

## Phase 3: Real-Time & n8n Automations (2026-10-07)

### Added
- Live block ticker (block, age, base fee, fullness) streamed over Server-Sent Events; pending transactions
  update when mined.
- Alerts (`/alerts`): ten types (wallet activity, gas, prices, validators, risky approvals, NFT floors, ENS
  expiry, depegs, governance, daily digest) on Telegram, Discord or email, with history.
- Alert pipeline: signed webhooks to n8n, Moralis Streams for real-time wallet alerts, de-duplicated events.
- n8n workflow exports and setup guide (`n8n/`); `/n8n-workflows` with Subscribe buttons.

## Phase 2: Data & Chain Expansion (2026-10-07)

### Added
- Base, Arbitrum, OP Mainnet, Polygon and Linea (plus Sepolia and Hoodi) across holdings, NFTs, portfolio,
  approvals and DeFi positions; `/l2` comparison and `/l2/[chain]` pages.
- Explorer pages: `/tx`, `/block`, `/address`, `/token`, with decoded transfers and address labels.
- New pages: `/defi`, `/dex-pools`, `/eth-supply`, `/blobs`, `/derivatives`, `/mev`, `/governance`, and a
  rebuilt `/eip-protocols` with an upgrade tracker.
- Token approvals, DeFi positions and a readable activity feed on `/me` and wallet pages; GoPlus risk badges.
- Homepage redesign and Cmd+K global search.

### Changed
- Navbar regrouped into Markets, Ethereum, Layer 2s, Wallets, Tokens & NFTs and More.

## Phase 1: Wallet Connection & Accounts (2026-10-07)

### Added
- Connect a wallet (MetaMask and other extensions, Coinbase Wallet, WalletConnect); the address fills in
  every wallet form.
- Sign-In with Ethereum with a secure session cookie; Neon Postgres and Drizzle for accounts.
- My Dashboard (`/me`): up to 5 saved wallets in one portfolio, value over time from daily snapshots, and CSV export.

## Phase 0: Foundation (2026-10-06)

### Changed
- Every data source moved to a free plan or keyless API; paid-only and shut-down endpoints replaced
  (CoinGecko Pro, Blocknative, Beaconcha.in, Alchemy NFT endpoints, Transpose and others).
- One client per provider with timeouts, retries, typed errors and caching; one key per provider.
- Zod validation and one error format on every route; `proxy.ts` blocks cross-site calls and rate-limits per IP.
- Docker image on Node 24 LTS; working lint, typecheck and GitHub Actions CI.

### Added
- Unit tests (Vitest), Sentry error monitoring and a shared Upstash Redis rate limit (all free tiers, optional).

### Fixed
- Retired Etherscan V1 endpoint, broken and dead routes, the Holesky testnet (replaced by Hoodi), a crash on
  unknown coins, forms that changed while typing, and unescaped text in feedback emails.

### Removed
- Unused routes and packages (Firecrawl, unused AI SDK providers and others).
